  "limitations": [
    "The caliper is a hand-read vernier without a calibration certificate; its stated maximum permissible error and the operator's reading resolution bound the standard, which is therefore not SI-traceable.",
    "One-dimensional per axis; axes are separate mountings, so absolute orthogonality between axes is not tested.",
    "Readings were typed by the operator before each hold and never inferred from camera data.",
    "The caliper sets the translation of the sliding jaw, not its tilt. A tilt of the jaw moves the camera centre in board coordinates by the working distance times the tilt, so the primary comparison uses the board centre in camera coordinates and the camera-centre comparison is reported alongside; the IMU on the jaw measures the tilt.",
    "The jaw tilt also moves the board centre by its offset from the caliper's measuring line times the tilt (Abbe); this remains in the residuals."
  ]
